7
00:00:29,700 --> 00:00:40,400
sent 29.7s for “brotherhood” (33.2s): The four men stop in a line in the dust, a long silent western standoff facing the house, then pull each other into an embrace.

8
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:45,500
sent 40.4s for “ears” (43.9s): One man rests his ear on his brother's chest; the donkeys wait.

9
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:50,300
sent 45.5s for “hilltops” (49.0s): Beyond them the hilltops and canyons of the mesas catch the last blinding light; the silver fog tower flares.

10
00:00:50,300 --> 00:00:55,100
sent 50.3s for “nights” (53.8s): Night falls: stars spread over the mesas, the fog tower glows soft blue, the men are lit by their glowing hourglasses.

11
00:00:55,100 --> 00:00:59,100
sent 55.1s for “laughter” (58.6s): The men are close now, laughing; she lights a fire in a clay brazier at the doorstep.

12
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:03,100
sent 59.1s for “football” (60.1s): A worn football is kicked through the firelight in the yard in front of her.

13
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,086
sent 63.1s for “home” (63.4s): The men reach the doorway and she embraces the poet; they are home.
